# Kaze example — greenhouse climate control.
#
#   This syntax example needs real sensor and alert backends that are not yet
#   available in the standalone built-in host; it must not simulate them.
#
# `fan` and `mister` are instances of the `device` family, so one grant
# covers both relays.

needs: sensor, fan, mister, alert

# Typed parameters carry their dimension, so the comparison below is checked
# against real units rather than trusted. A sensor read is fallible (the probe
# can be silent), so each read states what to use when it is.
check climate(target_temp: Celsius, target_humidity: percent):
    let temperature = sensor.temperature() otherwise 0 Celsius
    let humidity = sensor.humidity() otherwise 0%
    if temperature > target_temp + 2 Kelvin:
        turn on fan
        send alert "Cooling fan activated"
    otherwise:
        turn off fan
    if humidity < target_humidity:
        pulse mister for 5 seconds
